v0.4.1.9010
============

* reintroduced speaker_mismatch as an argument for `detect_speaker_regex_matches()` and `split_by_speakers()`
* minor adjustment in `get_agenda_item_calls()` to mirror the behaviour in the existing GermaParlTEIs in which the truncation of agenda items did not introduce an additional whitespace

v0.4.1.9009
============
* added more arguments to paragraphize() in utils to make paragraphs more adjustable
* fixed language argument so that setting NULL actually works
* added paragraph_by_whitespace argument to reconstruct_paragraphs() method to add an easier way to get paragraphs if working with pre-structured data

v0.4.1.9008
===========
* adjusted structural annotation to accommodate other TEI standards

v0.4.1.9007
===========
* Bug removed which concatenated non-interjection and interjection paragraphs resulting in missed interjection chunks.

v0.4.1.9005
===========
* matching for agenda_item_mismatch via id, not by filename (so that same mismatches can be used for xml-based and txt-based corpus preparation)
* Bug removed that occurs in PlenaryProtocolParser$make_body() when length of chunks is 1
* New field stage_mismatch_regex in PlenaryProtocolParser to prevent unwanted annotation of interjections.


v0.4.1.9004
===========
* Changes for a robust procedure when chunks are derived from XML
* When creating speaker attributes, regex/indext/text are dropped from attributes only if present; respective
check introduced in PlenaryProtocolParser$make_speaker_node()
* Speaker call is not necessarily there in chunk lines - respective check included.
* bug removed in PlenaryProtocolParser$save_xml() that would prevent it from working.

v0.4.1.9003
===========
* bug removed that occurred when concatenating multiple lines to match regex

v0.4.1.9001
===========
* data.frame with regex matches needs to be modified such that it does not break if no matches
* precautionary check in $make_body() to avoid empty paragraphs
* dependency on gsubfn (function strapplyc) has been dropped

v0.4.1
======
* new method $detect_stage_instructions
* all methods have been renamed to snake_case
* all params renamed to snake_case
* params to methods moved to fields, to reduce necessity to document params
* maxLengthWho argument replaced by field $speaker_maximum_nchar_name
* method $show_nchar_histogram() moved to auxiliary function hist_nchar()


v0.4.0
======
* birth given to frappp (a package formerly known as ctk.plpr)
* content of TODO file moved to issues of GermaParl package 
